            <TextBlock Text="Sessions shows observed clients and window controls. Choose Join a game there, or from Overview, to search and review a destination. Back to sessions returns to the same client view. Automation contains the saved macro catalog and assignments. Opening Join a game never starts a client, searches Roblox or enables previews." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,0,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="1. Build your account library" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="Open Accounts and choose + Add account. Complete sign-in on Roblox’s own page, then choose Save this Roblox sign-in. Zenith checks the player ID before creating an account named from its verified username. Closing sign-in before verification creates no account. If a save was already committed, cancellation preserves it for review. Already-saved Roblox identities require review rather than silently replacing their sign-in. Use Profile only… when you want optional local metadata without signing in. Select a row to edit notes, groups or preferences; these fields never authorize a launch. Group filters include all memberships. Manage groups reviews a rename or removal across the whole library, including accounts on other pages. Choose a fallback when removing a primary group; saved accounts and sign-ins stay in place. Existing target names require explicit merge approval and a new review. Editing names or a reviewed account invalidates the old review. Dense view fits more accounts, and metadata exports exclude sign-in material." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="Saved groups can be empty. In Manage groups, create a name, choose a named color or HEX value, and use Move up/down to organize the group list. Follow theme uses the current accent. Colors and group order do not change account priority, launches or sign-ins. Search and pages in the manager reach groups beyond the bounded filter suggestions. Profile metadata exports include membership names, but exclude empty groups, colors and group order." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,0,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="2. Understand profile and session identity" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="A profile is your local record. A session is an observed native process. A typed username does not prove which account a client uses. Sessions displays process identity and resources without claiming account or server information that has not been verified." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="3. Native game sessions" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="Account setup may use Roblox's sign-in page. Games must open in the native Roblox application, never in a browser window. Native account selection and launching are awaiting isolated verification; this preview does not substitute your browser's current account. Sessions → Focus requests foreground activation of an observed native window. Close asks only that selected, revalidated process window to close normally; a confirmation appears first." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="4. Preserve desktop headroom" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="Overview separates available physical RAM from system commit. Capacity estimates reserve spare memory and a provisional cost for each new client. Each queued request keeps its own physical and commit estimate; changing the defaults applies to new requests. The queue shows the pinned estimate. A recovered possible client without a recorded estimate needs closure review before another start. Unknown GPU values stay unavailable. A memory estimate never authorizes additional Roblox clients or proves background automation support." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="5. Settings, data, and recovery" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="Themes apply immediately. Save settings commits view and capacity preferences; the saved indicator changes only after writing succeeds. In Settings, use its search or Ctrl+F to find an existing control, then open a result. Search changes no preference or pending draft. Custom timing stays hidden until you explicitly choose Custom. User data stays outside the application folder. Export contains metadata only, never authorization. Imports create new local profiles and require sign-in separately. Preserve damaged files if a recovery error is reported." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="Destination favorites and links" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="In Sessions → Join a game, enter a public game name, place ID or supported game/server link and choose Search / Use. For a name, select a public result and choose Use selected experience; no result is chosen automatically. Browse public servers if needed, then use a selected server as your requested destination. Under Favorite destinations, enter a name and choose Save current as new. Use favorite restores that request without launching or contacting Roblox; Rename selected changes its name, and Remove selected asks for confirmation. Copy requested link copies IDs only. Favorites stay in your writable data folder, separate from account authorization, and do not reserve a server seat." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="Account bundles" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="In Accounts, check the profiles to save together. In Sessions → Join a game → Account bundles, enter a name and choose Save checked page as new. Switch account pages and use Add checked to bundle to extend the same bundle. Review members shows current profile existence and last-known player IDs. Missing profiles block the entire bundle request until you explicitly remove missing references or replace recipients. Choose a game or server link above, then Queue bundle for this destination. Recipients and target are pinned for that request; later bundle edits affect future requests. Native support, sign-in and capacity checks still apply to every account. Stop bundle work cancels preparation and pending requests it created; a client that may already have started still requires review." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="Native launch preparation inspection" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="Select an account with a saved Roblox sign-in. In Sessions → Join a game, choose a game-only destination, then Inspect and prevent launch. This opens a fresh private official game page using only the selected saved session. Choose Play there: Zenith cancels the external request and retains only known field labels, counts and the reported page-gesture flag. No ticket or full launch address is displayed or saved, and no native client starts. After browser cleanup, the page's current session must verify as the same player before it is saved. Cancelled, incomplete, mismatched or failed checks leave sign-in needing review or renewal. Panic, Lock and profile removal wait for the actual operation owner. A captured handoff does not prove native account selection, server arrival, simultaneous clients or reconnect support; those need separate live tests." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="Client CPU priority" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="In Sessions, open Client CPU priority. Check clients or select a row, then choose Normal or Below normal. Each operation pins those process instances and reports its result. Restore original affects the selected clients only while their observed priority matches Zenith's last change. Exit attempts to restore all changes made in this session. Windows can refuse a change or restoration. A crash can leave an applied priority until the client exits or you change it in Task Manager. Scheduling priority does not impose a CPU percentage, FPS or memory limit. Compare the same workload before deciding whether it helps." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="Explicit native account trials" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="For a scheduled compatibility test, select a native Roblox installation in Settings, a saved account in Accounts, and an explicit game or server in Sessions → Join a game. Review selected-account trial shows the selected account, place or server, and installation. Confirming allows that one reviewed request to use the unverified provider. Choose Play in its private Roblox page. Publisher, selected-account identity, saved authorization, resource headroom and stop controls are checked again before native startup. The queue shows the requested destination separately from the process receipt; neither proves the client's account or actual arrival. Pause, Panic, Lock, installation changes and restart revoke unstarted trial permission. Nothing resumes automatically. Review possible clients before confirming they are closed. Confirming closure releases only the forecast; any process Windows still observes remains counted." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="Use Launch evidence to inspect a pinned request. Requested player/place/server, the original process receipt, current process presence and separately timestamped log reports stay distinct. Reported match is still unverified; reported mismatch is a discrepancy to investigate. Teleport/disconnect and expired or ambiguous evidence never reuse last-known IDs as current. Show process selects the exact current process in Sessions; it sends no input. Copy/Save evidence exports only the displayed typed IDs and timing, not credentials, names, paths or raw logs. A startup stabilization countdown prevents rapid successive trials; fresh resources and explicit permission remain required after it ends." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,0,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="Client-start receipts and interrupted launches" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="A process-start receipt records the reported PID and creation time. It is not proof of the account, game arrival or current liveness. Client started · unverified remains reserved and reviewable; timeout or Panic cannot turn a late response into successful arrival. Use Review only after checking that no client or startup attempt remains. Restart restores pending work for review and never automatically relaunches it. Queue format4 preserves these receipts; older versions of the companion must not overwrite this newer queue." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="Arrange client windows" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="In Sessions, check clients or select one row. Minimize clients and Restore clients use that pinned selection without requiring a monitor choice; each state is confirmed separately. Restoring does not request foreground focus. Minimizing does not promise lower committed memory and minimized-window automation is unsupported. For tiling, choose Refresh monitors, select a monitor and check the clients to tile. With no checkboxes selected, Tile clients uses the selected row. Layout preferences set the gap, minimum outer-window size and optional column count in logical pixels; Windows scaling determines physical pixels. Each eligible normal, resizable window is checked again before moving. Restore minimized or maximized windows and leave fullscreen first. Arrangement does not request foreground focus. Cancel and Panic stop later requests but cannot undo a request already sent. The results list preserves per-client outcomes. Save all settings retains layout and your other preference edits; reopening the manager never automatically rearranges clients." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="Sessions → Content size uses physical content pixels, independently of the tiling preferences. Width starts at 640 and height at 480 on every manager launch. Tiny fills 320 × 240 only; choose Apply size to resize the checked clients, or the selected row when none are checked. Dimensions and recipients are pinned before work begins. Window frames add extra pixels, and each client uses its current monitor. Restore minimized or maximized clients and leave fullscreen first. Resizing does not request foreground activation, verify an account or prove automation compatibility. These temporary dimensions are never saved; Cancel, Lock and Panic stop later requests while retaining any reported partial outcomes." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,0,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="Resource history" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="Overview charts show measured machine CPU, available physical RAM and system commit. Sessions → History shows up to 120 samples over two minutes for the selected exact process instance. Select the client there or in Table. The chart axes use actual sample times and labelled shared memory/I/O scales. Missing, invalid, stale or reset measurements produce gaps, never invented zeroes. First process I/O readings warm up before a rate is available; changing PID/start identity cannot inherit an earlier instance's baseline. Read/write/other byte and operation rates combine files, network and devices, and do not measure disk-only activity, bandwidth or paging. Generic page faults combine soft and hard faults. History uses one shared reducer, no row-owned timers and no persisted running state. It is diagnostic information and does not verify an account, server or performance improvement. Returning to Table/History stops optional previews; history never starts capture or sends input." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="Windows overview" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="Choose Windows to see the observed clients tiled evenly inside Zenith. Start previews opts into one shared low-rate capture owner; Stop, leaving the page, hiding Zenith, Panic, Lock or resource pressure stops it. Every observed tile remains visible, including clients with no usable window. Incomplete discovery is labelled and is not proof that an absent client closed. Large groups refresh in fair small batches: the rate is shared, not a promise of one frame per second per client. A dated last-known picture is labelled separately from a current image and expires after two minutes. Select a tile to inspect it; Focus client is a separate explicit action. Selecting or clicking an image never sends game input, chooses macro recipients or proves the signed-in account. Saved accounts remain separate. Sessions → Tile clients arranges real desktop windows; Windows shows them inside the manager." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="Client previews" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="Previews are off on every launch. In Sessions → Table, check up to four observed clients or select one row. Choose Previews, then Preview checked clients. The process start time and window are pinned; changing checkboxes never silently retargets capture. Outputs fit 320 × 180 without upscaling and update no faster than once per second. Windows may capture at a higher internal rate and still reads the source surface; no resource-saving claim is implied. The Windows capture border stays enabled. Minimized, hidden, changed or unavailable windows show an explicit status. Old images expire after three seconds, are kept only in bounded memory and are never saved or used for input, identity verification or image matching. Leaving this view, hiding/minimizing Zenith, Lock, Panic, or unhealthy/stale resource measurements clears and stops previews. Return and Start explicitly to resume. Several large windows can exceed the shared surface budget and be deferred. Unsupported Windows capture has no desktop fallback. Roblox preview compatibility and live overhead still need real-client verification." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="Reported session destinations" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="Selected client details separates current diagnostic player/place/server values from timestamped last-known information. A process using a log is not proof of who wrote it, and these parser formats remain unverified. Copy reported server link checks the latest available evidence at the click and refuses expired, ambiguous or disconnected destinations. Copying does not establish public access, choose an authorized account or confirm a join." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="Recent client history" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="Expand Recent clients in Sessions to see up to100 process instances that a fresh, complete scan no longer observed. A partial, stale or failed scan does not establish absence. Each entry keeps the process start time and any last-reported, unverified player/game/server information. Zenith records a successful normal close request separately, but the actual cause of disappearance remains unknown. No historical row launches, rejoins, authorizes an account or restores running state. Clear recent history asks for confirmation and affects only ended records; active tracking continues. History uses a separate bounded client-history.db in your data folder. Save errors stay visible and require Retry history storage; damaged storage is preserved rather than replaced with an empty database. Use Open settings folder to locate and preserve that file before recovery." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="Official linking setup" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="On Accounts, create or select a saved profile, then choose Sign in with Roblox. Complete sign-in and security challenges on Roblox’s real page in the private window. Choose Save this Roblox sign-in only when the intended account is signed in. Zenith verifies the returned user ID before storing the reusable session with Windows protection. Check saved sign-in revalidates that same account; Remove saved sign-in deletes Zenith’s local authorization without deleting the profile or closing running games. Native account launch remains a separate capability. Existing older authorization records are preserved; reconnecting through this saved-sign-in flow requires explicitly removing an incompatible old link first." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="Account-link recovery" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="An expired or unreadable saved sign-in preserves the profile. Check saved sign-in contacts Roblox only for the selected protected account. An interrupted check requires fresh sign-in because Roblox may have replaced its session during the request. Cancel, Lock, Panic and Exit cancel the current attempt; the private page hides immediately while its owner finishes cleanup. Preserve unreadable protected files for recovery. Remove saved sign-in deletes only Zenith’s local authorization; it does not perform a global Roblox logout." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="Installed Roblox and bootstrappers" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" Margin="0,0,0,10" />
            <TextBlock Text="In Settings, Refresh installation reads bounded current-user registrations, standard locations and version metadata. It runs only when requested. Conflicting registrations or multiple versions remain visible; the app never guesses a preferred provider. Select a candidate to see its local path. Found files are unverified: installation discovery does not prove publisher trust, compatibility, account sign-in or native arrival. Cancel, Lock and Panic discard the current check; refresh explicitly after unlocking. No program, protocol registration or client file is changed. Portable or unregistered installations may be missed." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,0,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="Performance profiles" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" Margin="0,0,0,10" />
            <TextBlock Text="Choose a profile in Settings and save. Maximum Efficiency samples process details less often and spaces eligible starts further apart. Balanced keeps the normal cadence. High Performance refreshes manager observations more often, with additional monitoring overhead. Main Account Priority gives your explicitly selected saved profile a bounded launch-order boost while waiting-age fairness and admission stay active. Use as main account in the library chooses the profile; it does not verify a running client. Custom changes the displayed timing values within their ranges. Invalid custom timing remains pending; Reset custom timing restores valid defaults. Essential RAM, commit and CPU samples remain once per second and expire after three seconds. An active start keeps its original stabilization/spacing. Share manager performance settings exports only the profile and four custom timing values. Copy code or Save to file uses the current valid performance draft. Review code or Review file shows the profile, effective policy and dormant custom values; Use in draft changes only those fields while keeping your current main account. Save settings is still required. Share codes are readable and unauthenticated; imported values still have to pass validation. No account, authorization, safety headroom, hotkey, layout or client flag is transferred. No profile promises game FPS or client-capacity gains; unsupported graphics, FPS, client CPU/render, previews and macro policies remain pending." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,0,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="{Binding PanicShortcutStatus}" Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,14" />
            <TextBlock Text="{Binding DiagnosticsStatus}" Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,0,0,20" />
            <TextBlock Text="Diagnostics and navigation" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" Margin="0,0,0,10" />
            <TextBlock Text="Ctrl+1–7 switches the seven sidebar sections while this manager is focused. These local navigation keys do not register global shortcuts or replace Zenith transport bindings. Diagnostics shows the newest 512 manager events and session totals. Pause view freezes display only. Clear view hides current entries without deleting logs. Severity and text filters apply to Copy visible and the redacted report. Save report writes a JSON file outside application/data folders. Reports omit account metadata, paths, URLs, settings, credentials and raw exception messages; nothing is uploaded. The live view covers this launch only; Open logs shows the retained rotating files." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,0,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="6. Account avatars and server destinations" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" Margin="0,0,0,10" />
            <TextBlock Text="Use Choose server in Account details to open Join a game. Use the account's … menu to refresh its public avatar or use its preferred game. In Sessions, Review reported server fills the destination field when a current client reports a server. Choose Search / Use to review that request. Headshots load for verified player IDs while the Accounts page is visible, using one shared bounded loader. Use Refresh public avatar to retry. Sample profiles do not contact Roblox. Public names and pictures do not prove a current sign-in or identify a local process. In Sessions → Join a game, enter a public name, place ID or supported game/server link and choose Search / Use. A successful explicit choice loads details; Load game details can refresh them to see its public name, creator, experience-wide players and requested/root place IDs; loading details never replaces your requested place. The icon is optional and validated before display. The experience gallery preserves public media order; use Previous and Next to browse. Pending, unavailable and unsupported video items have explicit states. These pictures are experience artwork, not live client frames. Browse public servers one page at a time, select one, and press Use selected server before Queue checked accounts. Capacity advice compares that observation with the checked recipients, or the selected account when none are checked. It expires after five minutes; reported slots are not reserved seats. Recipients and destination are frozen before queuing; unavailable providers produce blocked requests. Private/share codes are discarded and never guessed into a public destination. A queued request is not confirmed arrival." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,0,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="7. Platform capabilities and stopping" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="Automation lists supported, unavailable, and unverified functionality. Native diagnostic successes are not Roblox compatibility. Panic stop is always available and leaves clients open. Lock hides account controls while monitoring continues. Closing the main window keeps the manager in the tray; use the tray menu's Exit command to shut it down." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="Saved macros from Personal Zenith" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="Open the matching Personal Zenith build, then choose Automation → Saved macros → Refresh host macros. The list shows successfully saved or loaded macros and their assigned shortcuts, rather than pending edits. Previous and Next browse one page at a time. If Zenith changes its library while you browse, refresh from the beginning. Connection failures keep the last received page clearly marked as stale. This connection does not copy macro contents, start the editor automatically or run playback. Shared playback and broadcasting remain unavailable until their integrations and real-client tests pass. Sample mode does not connect to your real macro library." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="Shared macro assignments" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="In Automation, refresh saved macros and assignments. Select a saved macro, then choose Selected account, Current saved group or Selected bundle to pin the target shown in the assignment panel. Assign checks that target's stable ID and rechecks the received host page before saving one macro reference. Later selection changes never redirect a pending request. A group or bundle's members will be resolved and frozen at a future explicit run start. Last-observed names are hints: a removed group or off-page macro is never replaced by another with the same name. Remove assignment deletes only that reference, after checking the confirmation box. Conflicting changes require Refresh; cancelled requests may already have committed metadata, so refresh to inspect them. Assignments survive restarts but never resume playback. Macro execution and live account/provider verification remain unfinished." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
            <TextBlock Text="8. Interrupted saves and recovery" Style="{StaticResource SectionTitle}" />
            <TextBlock Text="A missing or damaged main queue can load its verified backup for review. Recovered requests remain paused; no client or macro restarts automatically. The startup notice and Log identify backup recovery. Saved settings can also load a verified backup without immediately replacing your original files. If recovery is blocked, keep the .bak, .tmp and .damaged files and use Settings to open the data folder for review. Do not delete them to dismiss a warning. Unsupported newer files need a compatible app version. Account profiles remain usable when the separate launch queue is unavailable." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" Margin="0,10,0,24" />
          </StackPanel>
        </ScrollViewer>
      </Grid>
      <!-- One footer: launch-queue state + notices. Expanding opens the queue above it. -->
      <Expander Grid.Row="2" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" IsExpanded="{Binding QueueExpanded}" AutomationProperties.Name="Launch queue">
        <Expander.Template>
          <ControlTemplate TargetType="Expander">
            <Border Background="{DynamicResource HeaderBackground}" BorderBrush="{DynamicResource BorderBrushLight}" BorderThickness="0,1,0,0">
              <DockPanel>
                <Grid DockPanel.Dock="Bottom" MinHeight="34">
                  <Grid.ColumnDefinitions><ColumnDefinition Width="Auto" /><ColumnDefinition Width="*" /></Grid.ColumnDefinitions>
                  <ToggleButton IsChecked="{Binding IsExpanded, RelativeSource={RelativeSource TemplatedParent}, Mode=TwoWay}" Cursor="Hand" FocusVisualStyle="{StaticResource KeyboardFocusRing}" ToolTip="Show or hide the launch queue" AutomationProperties.Name="Show launch queue">
                    <ToggleButton.Template>
                      <ControlTemplate TargetType="ToggleButton">
                        <Border x:Name="Hit" Background="Transparent" Padding="14,0,6,0">
                          <Path x:Name="Chevron" Width="12" Height="12" Stretch="Uniform" Data="M 3,10 L 8,5 L 13,10" Stroke="{DynamicResource TextSecondary}" StrokeThickness="1.5" StrokeStartLineCap="Round" StrokeEndLineCap="Round" StrokeLineJoin="Round" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                        </Border>
                        <ControlTemplate.Triggers>
                          <Trigger Property="IsChecked" Value="True"><Setter TargetName="Chevron" Property="Data" Value="M 3,6 L 8,11 L 13,6" /></Trigger>
                          <Trigger Property="IsMouseOver" Value="True"><Setter TargetName="Hit" Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource HoverBackground}" /></Trigger>
                        </ControlTemplate.Triggers>
                      </ControlTemplate>
                    </ToggleButton.Template>
                  </ToggleButton>
                  <ContentPresenter Grid.Column="1" ContentSource="Header" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
                </Grid>
                <ContentPresenter x:Name="ExpandedContent" Visibility="Collapsed" ContentSource="Content" />
              </DockPanel>
            </Border>
            <ControlTemplate.Triggers>
              <Trigger Property="IsExpanded" Value="True"><Setter TargetName="ExpandedContent" Property="Visibility" Value="Visible" /></Trigger>
            </ControlTemplate.Triggers>
          </ControlTemplate>
        </Expander.Template>
        <Expander.Header>
          <DockPanel LastChildFill="True" MinHeight="32" Margin="4,0,0,0">
            <Button DockPanel.Dock="Right" Content="{Binding QueuePauseLabel}" Command="{Binding ToggleQueuePause}" IsEnabled="{Binding QueueReady}" MinHeight="26" Padding="10,0" Margin="12,2,8,2" />
            <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Right" Text="{Binding SaveStatus}" Style="{StaticResource CaptionLine}" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="16,0,0,0" />
            <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Left" Text="Launch queue" FontWeight="SemiBold" FontSize="12" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,10,0" />
            <ContentControl DockPanel.Dock="Left" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,12,0">
              <ContentControl.Style>
                <Style TargetType="ContentControl" BasedOn="{StaticResource ChipSuccess}">
                  <Setter Property="Content" Value="Active" />
                  <Style.Triggers>
                    <DataTrigger Binding="{Binding QueuePauseLabel}" Value="Resume queue"><Setter Property="Content" Value="Paused" /><Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource BadgeBgWarning}" /><Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource BadgeBgWarning}" /><Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource AccentWarning}" /></DataTrigger>
                    <DataTrigger Binding="{Binding QueueReady}" Value="False"><Setter Property="Content" Value="Opening" /><Setter Property="Background" Value="{DynamicResource SurfaceBackground}" /><Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="{DynamicResource SurfaceBackground}" /><Setter Property="Foreground" Value="{DynamicResource TextSecondary}" /></DataTrigger>
                  </Style.Triggers>
                </Style>
              </ContentControl.Style>
            </ContentControl>
            <TextBlock DockPanel.Dock="Left" Text="{Binding QueueStatus}" ToolTip="{Binding QueueStatus}" Style="{StaticResource CaptionLine}" MaxWidth="420" VerticalAlignment="Center" Margin="0,0,16,0" />
            <TextBlock Text="{Binding Notice}" ToolTip="{Binding Notice}" Style="{StaticResource CaptionLine}" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextSecondary}" VerticalAlignment="Center" />
          </DockPanel>
        </Expander.Header>
        <Grid Height="220" Margin="16,10,16,6">
          <ListView ItemsSource="{Binding Launches}" Background="{DynamicResource CardBackground}" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextPrimary}" BorderBrush="{DynamicResource BorderBrushLight}" VirtualizingPanel.IsVirtualizing="True" VirtualizingPanel.VirtualizationMode="Recycling" ScrollViewer.CanContentScroll="True" AutomationProperties.Name="Launch requests">
            <ListView.View>
              <GridView>
                <GridViewColumn Header="Account / process" Width="225"><GridViewColumn.CellTemplate><DataTemplate><StackPanel><TextBlock Text="{Binding Label}" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" ToolTip="{Binding Label}" /><TextBlock Text="{Binding ProcessReceipt}" ToolTip="{Binding ProcessReceipt}" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" FontSize="11" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextSecondary}" Margin="0,3,0,0" /><TextBlock Text="{Binding ResourceEstimate}" ToolTip="{Binding ResourceEstimate}" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" FontSize="11" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextMuted}" Margin="0,3,0,0" /></StackPanel></DataTemplate></GridViewColumn.CellTemplate></GridViewColumn>
                <GridViewColumn Header="State" Width="145"><GridViewColumn.CellTemplate><DataTemplate><TextBlock Text="{Binding State}" TextWrapping="Wrap" /></DataTemplate></GridViewColumn.CellTemplate></GridViewColumn>
                <GridViewColumn Header="Destination" Width="230"><GridViewColumn.CellTemplate><DataTemplate><TextBlock Text="{Binding RequestedDestination}" ToolTip="{Binding RequestedDestination}" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" /></DataTemplate></GridViewColumn.CellTemplate></GridViewColumn>
                <GridViewColumn Header="Details" Width="290"><GridViewColumn.CellTemplate><DataTemplate><TextBlock Text="{Binding Detail}" ToolTip="{Binding Detail}" TextTrimming="CharacterEllipsis" Foreground="{DynamicResource TextSecondary}" /></DataTemplate></GridViewColumn.CellTemplate></GridViewColumn>
                <GridViewColumn Header="" Width="160">
                  <GridViewColumn.CellTemplate>
                    <DataTemplate>
                      <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal">
                        <Button Content="Cancel" Command="{Binding DataContext.CancelLaunch, RelativeSource={RelativeSource AncestorType=Window}}" CommandParameter="{Binding}" IsEnabled="{Binding CanCancel}" Style="{StaticResource QuietButton}" Padding="10,0" />
                        <Button Content="Review" Click="ReviewLaunch" IsEnabled="{Binding CanReview}" Padding="10,0" Margin="6,0,0,0" />
                      </StackPanel>
                    </DataTemplate>
                  </GridViewColumn.CellTemplate>
                </GridViewColumn>
              </GridView>
            </ListView.View>
          </ListView>
          <TextBlock Text="No launch requests yet. Queue an account's preferred game, or pick a game in Join a game." HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" TextAlignment="Center" MaxWidth="560" IsHitTestVisible="False">
            <TextBlock.Style>
              <Style TargetType="TextBlock" BasedOn="{StaticResource Muted}">
                <Setter Property="Visibility" Value="Collapsed" />
                <Style.Triggers><DataTrigger Binding="{Binding Launches.Count}" Value="0"><Setter Property="Visibility" Value="Visible" /></DataTrigger></Style.Triggers>
              </Style>
            </TextBlock.Style>
          </TextBlock>
        </Grid>
      </Expander>
      <Border Grid.Row="1" Grid.RowSpan="2" Grid.ColumnSpan="2" Background="{DynamicResource AppBackground}" Visibility="{Binding IsLocked, Converter={StaticResource VisibleIf}}">
        <StackPanel HorizontalAlignment="Center" VerticalAlignment="Center" Width="420">
          <theme:ThemeAwareLogo Width="48" Height="48" HorizontalAlignment="Left" />
          <TextBlock Text="Controls are locked" Style="{StaticResource PageTitle}" Margin="0,20,0,10" />
          <TextBlock Text="Account details are hidden. Monitoring continues; automation and reconnect require an explicit restart after unlocking." Style="{StaticResource Muted}" />
          <Button Content="Unlock dashboard" Command="{Binding Unlock}" Style="{StaticResource PrimaryButton}" HorizontalAlignment="Left" Margin="0,22,0,0" />
          <Expander Header="Close a running client safely" Margin="0,20,0,0">
            <ScrollViewer MaxHeight="220" VerticalScrollBarVisibility="Auto">
              <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{Binding Sessions}">
                <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                  <DataTemplate><DockPanel Margin="0,6"><Button Content="Close client" DockPanel.Dock="Right" Click="CloseSession" Margin="8,0,0,0" /><TextBlock Text="{Binding ProcessLabel}" VerticalAlignment="Center" /></DockPanel></DataTemplate>
                </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
              </ItemsControl>
            </ScrollViewer>
          </Expander>
        </StackPanel>
      </Border>
    </Grid>
  </Border>
</Window>
